The cost per gallon of lemonade includes both the cost of lemons and sugar. Given that it costs $3 for lemons and $2 for sugar per gallon, the total cost per gallon is:

\[ \text{Cost per gallon} = \$3 + \$2 = \$5 \]

This cost per gallon relates to the total cost calculation because if you know how many gallons were made, you can multiply that by the cost per gallon to find the total cost. For example, if they made 10 gallons of lemonade, the total cost would be:

\[ \text{Total cost} = 10 \times \$5 = \$50 \]

